    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Born a dwarf in nineteenth-century England, Ephraim Wainwright was ghouled and then Embraced by the Tremere Aidan Lyle after proving his mastery of Thaumaturgical theory. A scholar's scholar with a reputation for apocalyptic writing (his Songs of the Eve of Gehenna scandalized both Camarilla and Tremere elders alike), Wainwright now presides over the Annex at the Kenilworth, the largest of New York's satellite chantries, where his Kenilworth thaumaturges have lately turned their study toward rituals &mdash; including Blood Into Water, Luminous Vitae, and Obscure the Malice &mdash; that shore up the Masquerade in the war's aftermath. Secretly tasked by Vienna to engineer High Regent Aisling Sturbridge's downfall, Wainwright resents answering to both Sturbridge and the upstart Eugenio Estevez.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>You tolerate no dissent from those beneath you and consider undermining Sturbridge a matter of clan discipline, not treachery. Younger Tremere's fondness for &ldquo;technomancies&rdquo; and other bastard sorceries offends you personally.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Aidan Lyle. Thaumaturgical Paths (Storyteller discretion): Path of Blood 5, Alchemy 5, Lure of Flames 5, Movement of the Mind 5, Path of Conjuring 5, Countermagic 4, The Hearth Path 4, Elemental Mastery 3, Spirit Manipulation 3, Focused Mind 2. Secretly tasked by Vienna to unseat Aisling Sturbridge. Ratings above 5 from the original stat block have been capped to fit this system's 1-5 scale.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
